cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Replication package for: Arbitrage-Constrained Neural Interpolation of the Implied Volatility Surface: Evidence from NSE Index Options"
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: Jain
    given-names: Pramukh Rajendra
    affiliation: "School of Computer Science and Engineering, Vellore Institute of Technology, Chennai, India"
  - family-names: Sinha
    given-names: Mallika
    affiliation: "School of Social Sciences and Languages, Vellore Institute of Technology, Chennai, India"
    email: mallika.sinha@vit.ac.in
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7918-820X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pramukhjain123/nifty-iv-surface"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Code and derived data behind PNmix (prior-network mixture), an implied
  volatility surface for NIFTY 50 index options that is free of butterfly and
  calendar arbitrage by construction. The package builds the evaluation panel
  from NSE F&O bhavcopy files (2020-2026), fits PNmix and the benchmark
  methods (SVI, SSVI, Fengler's smoother, thin-plate and cubic splines) on
  18 expanding-origin folds, and reproduces every table and figure in the
  paper, including the intraday backtest in Section VII.
keywords:
  - implied volatility surface
  - no-arbitrage constraints
  - neural networks
  - lognormal mixtures
  - quadratic programming
  - NIFTY 50
  - NSE
  - index options
